Integration tests for cadc-tap that run against the CADC youcat service.

Requirements
------------

* Authorization to access the youcat service on the target host.
* A dedicated database schema for the tests (tables are created and deleted
  in this schema during the run).
* A directory containing three client certificate files (see below).
* Test users represented by the auth certificates must be members of the
  CADC_TEST2-Staff group (used for group read/write permission checks).

Environment variables
---------------------

CADCTAP_SCHEMA (required)
    Name of the database schema to use for the tests, e.g. int_test_schema.

CADC_CERT_DIR (required)
    Path to a directory that contains the certificate files listed below.

TAP_HOST (optional)
    Host name of the youcat TAP service. A plain hostname or a URL with an
    optional https:// scheme is accepted (e.g. ws.cadc-ccda.hia-iha.nrc-cnrc.gc.ca
    or https://ws.cadc-ccda.hia-iha.nrc-cnrc.gc.ca). Defaults to the CADC
    registry host when not set.

Certificate directory
---------------------

Set CADC_CERT_DIR to a directory that contains these three PEM files:

cadc-tap-test-auth1.pem
    Primary authenticated test user. Owns the test schema and tables for
    most operations. Must be a member of CADC_TEST2-Staff.

cadc-tap-test-auth2.pem
    Second authenticated test user. Used for cross-user permission checks.
    Must be a member of CADC_TEST2-Staff.

cadc-tap-test-reg.pem
    Registered CADC user that is not a member of CADC_TEST2-Staff. Used to
    verify that users outside the group are denied access when expected.

The tests refer to these files by the names above. They are typically
symlinks to standard CADC test certificates.

Owner names used in permission assertions are derived automatically from
each certificate at startup (CADC username from the certificate CN).

Running the tests
-----------------

From the cadctap package directory:

    CADCTAP_SCHEMA=int_test_schema \
    CADC_CERT_DIR=/path/to/test-certificates \
    pytest intTest/test_all.py -v

To follow step-by-step progress and see timing for each CLI call (useful
when diagnosing slow runs or hangs):

    CADCTAP_SCHEMA=int_test_schema \
    CADC_CERT_DIR=/path/to/test-certificates \
    pytest intTest/test_all.py -v -s --log-cli-level=INFO

Each test step logs lines of the form:

    >>> STEP N START: <description>
    <<< STEP N DONE:  <description> (<seconds>s)

If a run appears to hang, the last START line without a matching DONE line
indicates where it is stuck.
